---
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
import ContentCard from '../../components/ContentCard.astro';
import DocumentLayout from '../../layouts/DocumentLayout.astro';
const version = '0.1.0-draft.1';
const artifactPath = `/core/${version}`;
const title = 'TENSOR Core';
const description = 'A candidate shared contract for portable cyber investigations, usable by humans and agents.';
---

<DocumentLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/core/">
  <ContentCard>
<p class="section-kicker">Core 0.1.0-draft.1 · Implementation candidate</p>
    <h2>The shared investigation model</h2>
    <p>TENSOR Core defines how a cyber investigation records questions, evidence references, observations, hypotheses, assessments, decisions, and actions. The same model applies to human investigators, agents, and mixed teams.</p>
    <p>A reusable definition describes a question and its criteria. An investigation record applies that definition to specific subjects and times, with attributed assessments and a retained history. A bundle carries the record and its exact definition artifacts between tools.</p>
    <div class="cta-group"><Button variant="primary" href="/implement/">Implementation guide</Button><Button variant="secondary" href="/investigation-lab/">Open example investigations</Button></div>

    <h2>Core, graphs, and layers</h2>
    <ol class="layers" aria-label="TENSOR architecture layers">
      <li><strong>Vendor and organization graphs</strong><span>Product knowledge, data-source mappings, additional questions, policy, and operational workflows.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Public investigation graphs and profiles</strong><span>Shared technical questions, evidence criteria, and routes across cyber domains.</span></li>
      <li><strong>TENSOR Core</strong><span>Identity, context, attribution, assessments, decisions, revision history, and exchange rules.</span></li>
    </ol>
    <p><a href="/extensions/">Vendor and organization layers</a> extend the public foundation with explicit ownership, versions, and dependencies. Product procedures and business decisions remain distinguishable from technical findings.</p>
    <p>The <a href="/graphs/">working public graph</a> contains 609 questions: all 588 original IDs and 21 additional repair questions. The <a href="/graphs/coverage/">coverage ledger</a> records revised meaning and review status. This graph format and the Core record binding are separate contracts.</p>

    <h2>Contract and binding</h2>
    <div class="resource-grid">
      <section><h3>Specification documents</h3><ul>
        <li><a href="/founding/01-core-contract.md">Logical Core contract · 38 requirements</a></li>
        <li><a href="/founding/00-charter.md">Founding charter</a></li>
        <li><a href="/founding/02-governance.md">Governance proposal</a></li>
        <li><a href="/founding/03-standards-crosswalk.md">Standards crosswalk</a></li>
      </ul></section>
      <section><h3>JSON binding {version}</h3><ul>
        <li><a href={`${artifactPath}/binding.md`}>Binding rules</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${artifactPath}/schemas/bundle.schema.json`}>Bundle schema</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${artifactPath}/schemas/definition.schema.json`}>Definition schema</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${artifactPath}/schemas/record.schema.json`}>Record schema</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${artifactPath}/coverage.md`}>Validator coverage</a></li>
      </ul></section>
    </div>
    <p>The logical contract defines the proposed requirements. The binding specifies their JSON representation and interpretation. The reference validator checks the supported structural and semantic rules.</p>

    <h2>Reference investigations</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href={`${artifactPath}/examples/case-a.bundle.json`} download>Agent transfer · JSON bundle</a> — a human-led investigation with an initially unknown assessment, new evidence, and a revision.</li>
      <li><a href={`${artifactPath}/examples/case-b.bundle.json`} download>Identity incident · JSON bundle</a> — an agent-assisted investigation with competing explanations and a human handoff.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>These illustrative cases contain fictional actors, policies, and evidence references. The <a href="/investigation-lab/">Investigation Lab</a> provides inspection, validation, replay, export, and reimport.</p>

    <h2>Version and status</h2>
    <p>Core {version} is an unratified implementation candidate. The <a href="/review/">technical review package</a> pins its source and baseline. Independent exchange, external review, and stable-release decisions remain open. <a href="/conformance/">Validation documentation</a> defines the scope of an implementation result.</p>
  </ContentCard>
</DocumentLayout>
